# The Cornell box (docs/apps/raytrace.md, "Example scenes"): the walls, the blocks, the light and the
# camera as the Cornell Program of Computer Graphics measured them, in millimetres at a hundredth
# (www.graphics.cornell.edu/online/box/data.html); the colours as RGB of its spectra, the light's
# as 17, 12, 4. The camera: 35 mm of lens over 25 mm of film, at 278 273 -800 looking along z.
camera target 2.78 2.73 2.796 turn 180 tilt 0 far 10.796 lens 0.357143
background power 0
object "White walls" cornell-white.obj scale 0.01 colour 0.725 0.71 0.68
object "Red wall" cornell-red.obj scale 0.01 colour 0.63 0.065 0.05
object "Green wall" cornell-green.obj scale 0.01 colour 0.14 0.45 0.091
object "Short block" cornell-short.obj scale 0.01 colour 0.725 0.71 0.68
object "Tall block" cornell-tall.obj scale 0.01 colour 0.725 0.71 0.68
object "Light" cornell-light.obj scale 0.01 kind glow colour 1 0.706 0.235 glow 17
